          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first player to empty your hand of all cards.',
          gameplay: "1. **Establish Rank**: A target rank (e.g., Queens) is chosen for the round. 2. **Turn**: Each player in turn must play 1 to 4 cards face-down, claiming they are the target rank. 3. **Challenge**: Any player can shout 'Bluff!' or 'I Doubt It!' after a play. 4. **Reveal**: If challenged, the played cards are revealed. 5. **Penalty**: If the player lied, they take the entire table pile. If they were truthful, the challenger takes the pile. 6. **Rank Change**: The rank changes to the next in sequence (A-2-3...) after a successful challenge or when a new round starts.",
          keyRules: [
            'You must play at least one card every turn.',
            "Any player can challenge any other player's claim.",
            'Successful challenges reset the central pile.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Only bluff when you have no choice or when you hold very few cards of the current rank. Use your real cards first to thin your hand.',
          intermediate: 'Rank Tracking: Count how many cards of the current rank have been played. If you hold three Kings and someone else plays two, you know they are lying.',
          advanced: "The Desperation Bluff: If you are down to your last card and it doesn't match the rank, you MUST bluff. Try to play it quickly and confidently to deter challenges.",
          tips: [
            "Watch for 'Hesitation Tells'—players often pause longer when they are about to lie.",
            'If you win a challenge and set the next rank, choose one where you hold several cards.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
