          deckDescription: 'One standard 52-card deck consisting of four suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs), each with thirteen ranks from ace down to two. No jokers; used for Bluff (Cheat) where players claim ranks and may lie; suits are ignored.',
          suitDescription: 'Four French suits (spades, hearts, diamonds, clubs). Suits have no effect on play; only the rank of the card matters. Players play in rank order (twos, then threes, etc.); claiming a rank that does not match is the bluff.',
          rankDescription: 'Thirteen ranks per suit (ace through two). Play proceeds in rank order; the current rank to play determines what may be laid. Face cards and aces follow the same order. Matching the declared rank or bluffing is the core of the game.',
          dealPattern: 'Cards are dealt one at a time clockwise until the deck is exhausted.',
          bettingLimits: 'None',
          actions: {},
          handRankingSystem: 'None; card ranks are used for matching claims rather than comparative strength.',
          rankingSystem: 'Rank Sequential (A-2-3...)',
          useTrump: false,
          notApplicableReasons: {
            drawConfig: 'The full deck is distributed at the start; new cards are obtained only via challenge penalties.',
            discardConfig: 'Cards are played face-down to the center pile; no separate waste or discard pile exists.',
            specialCards: 'All cards follow the standard rank sequence; no individual card has a secondary engine effect.',
            declarationMechanism: 'Challenges are performed verbally; no hidden tokens or chips are used for declarations.',
            fishingConfig: 'Bluff is a shedding game and does not use a capture-from-tableau fishing mechanic.',
            trickConfig: 'Bluff uses a turn-based shedding loop rather than a trick-taking competition.',
          },
        },
